course: dictionary
lesson: 3958
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «Furnish» is a verb with two meanings. In everyday life, to furnish a room means to put furniture in it, such as beds, tables and chairs.
explain: In a formal voice, furnish means to supply or give something needed. «The school will furnish us with the details» means the school will give us the details. Ask yourself: is this about things in a room, or about giving information?
explain: «Hard bare walls bounce sound back, while soft curtains, carpets and sofas soak it up, so a furnished room hardly echoes.» The sentence gives the clues: curtains, carpets and sofas are soft, and they stop sound bouncing back. So furnished means a room with furniture in it.
fact: Furnish is a verb: furnish, furnishes, furnished, furnishing.
fact: «Furnish» means to put furniture in a room or house, as in «They furnished the bedroom.»
fact: A «furnished flat» comes with beds, tables and chairs already in it.
fact: Formal «furnish» means to supply or give something needed, as in «furnish us with the details».
fact: «Fully furnished» means every room has all its furniture.
exercise: «They furnished the bedroom.» What does furnished mean here? | Cleaned the windows | *Put furniture in the room | Painted the walls green | Locked the door
exercise: The letter says, «We will furnish you with the details.» What does furnish mean here? | Sing loudly | Lose | *Give something needed | Hide
exercise: Ella reads «a fully furnished flat». What does this suggest? | *A flat with all its furniture already in it | An empty flat with no furniture | A flat far away at the top of a hill | A flat that is on fire
test: «The hall was furnished with a long table and twelve chairs.» What does furnished mean? | Quiet and empty | Decorated with paint | Made of wood | *Had furniture put in
test: Mum says, «Can you furnish me with the address?» What does furnish mean? | Hide | *Supply, or give | Break | Sing
exam: Jayden reads «Hard bare walls bounce sound back, while soft curtains, carpets and sofas soak it up, so a furnished room hardly echoes.» What does furnished mean? | Made of stone | *Full of furniture such as carpets, curtains and sofas | Empty and bare | Painted in bright colours
